ll are distinct positive integers: `4, 6, 7, 8, 15`.<br>- They are in ascending order: ~~4 < 6 < 7 < 8 < 15~~.<br>- The sum of the two smallest is ~~4 + 6 = 10~~ (consistent with Statement 2).<br>- The sum of the three largest is ~~7 + 8 + 15 = 30~~ (consistent with Statement 1).<br>The sum of this set is indeed ~~4 + 6 + 7 + 8 + 15 = 40~~, and its average is ~~40 / 5 = 8~~. Since the combined information uniquely determines the total sum of the integers to be 40, the average is also uniquely determined to be 8.<br><br><strong>Final Answer</strong><br>Statement (1) alone is not sufficient. Statement (2) alone is not sufficient. However, when both statements are considered together, the sum of all five integers can be uniquely determined, which in turn uniquely determines their average. Therefore, BOTH statements TOGETHER are sufficient.<br>The final answer is C."
